<title>POLAND: Polish life insurers 1996 premiums up 50 pct - poll.</title>
<headline>Polish life insurers 1996 premiums up 50 pct - poll.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish life insurance firms collected 2.79 billion zlotys in gross premiums in 1996, over 50 percent more than in 1995, a poll by Nowa Europa financial daily showed.</p>
<p>According to the poll 11 life insurance firms had a total net profit of 109.9 million zlotys, 71 percent higher than in 1995. It said six firms had losses and five showed profits.</p>
<p>The poll also showed that  Powszechny Zaklad Ubezpieczen na Zycie SA, a subsidiary of state-owned PZU SA, had 77.1 percent of the domestic life insurance market and Polish unit of British Commercial Union had 11.6 percent.</p>
<p>It also said Amplico Life, a joint venture of U.S.-based American Insurance Group (AIG) and Polish state-owned Bank Pekao SA had 7.4 percent of the market. The remaining firms had below five percent market share.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
